WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.990
A sealed flask holds a mixture
of reactants and products.

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:05.890
Nothing seems to be happening.

3
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.090
It looks completely still.

4
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.030
Is it already at equilibrium?

5
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.570
Or is it quietly reacting,
one way or the other?

6
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.190
A sealed flask looks unchanging.

7
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.530
Can you tell which way it will react?

8
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:20.770
In this mission, you'll build ICE tables,

9
00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.150
and use them to calculate
equilibrium constants.

10
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:28.630
You'll handle reactions with a very
small K, and link K to Gibbs energy.

11
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:34.270
Your mission: work out whether you can
tell which way a sealed flask will react.
